filter-env oracle case: captured-helper-unpack-install

Isolates the real end-of-phase save after src_install (same
--filter-features call shape as every other phase end): the
2378-byte captured pattern over the install-phase declare dump
(image populated, build-info written just before).
If the native port regressed on any line kind in this dump, out
would differ byte-for-byte.

Run exactly as the phase runtime runs it:
  /usr/bin/python <checkout>/bin/filter-bash-environment.py "$(cat args)" < in > out 2> stderr.txt
Byte-exact: the args file bytes are argv[1] (no trailing newline
added, none present); the in file bytes are stdin verbatim.

Provenance (D4):
  portage-ref: portage-3.0.82.2
  portage-commit: 1d95fc2c552a2c7d347e54093fa0e5b172a57004 (3rdparty/repos.toml [portage] commit)
  python: Python 3.14.8 (/usr/bin/python)
  capture: instrumented real Portage in bed container
    localhost/test-portuale:latest (Portage 3.0.82.2, container python 3.14.6)
    with bin/filter-bash-environment.py replaced by a logging
    wrapper (argv[1] + stdin recorded per call, then the real
    script re-executed with identical argv + stdin).
    ebuild | command | EBUILD_PHASE: porttest/porttest/helper-unpack/helper-unpack-1.0.ebuild | install | install
    EMERGE_FROM=ebuild (the ebuild(1) branch, same pattern
    branch as a source merge; the binary-merge branch and the
    preprocess --filter-locale/--filter-path/--filter-sandbox
    option set did not occur in these runs).
  sizes: args=2378 in=22534 out=11840
  date: 2026-10-08 (UTC day granularity; the only field that may change
